by Amoifr at 2026-08-21T07:50:17Z

Thanks a lot for the thorough testing @mlwymore, this is exactly the kind of feedback the PR needed! Everything below is pushed in 4e13f708.

**Dropdown menu**

- `<button {{ ...dropdown_menu_trigger_attrs }}>`: the `{{ ... }}` spread is a Twig Components feature, it only works on `<twig:...>` tags. On a plain HTML element it reaches Twig as-is and blows up at compile time, as you saw. The way to do it is `<button type="button" {{ html_attr(dropdown_menu_trigger_attrs) }}>`. I added that to the README right after the usage example (and the same trap exists in the upstream `hover-card` README, I will fix it separately).
- `<twig:ux:icon ... {{ ...dropdown_menu_trigger_attrs }} />`: that one is a limitation of `ux:icon` itself, which rejects the typed attribute values the Toolkit uses for `data-action` merging. It is not specific to this recipe (any `*_trigger_attrs` hits it), so it deserves its own fix on the Icons side. In practice an `<svg>` is not a good trigger anyway (not focusable, no keyboard activation), so wrapping the icon in a `<twig:Button variant="ghost" size="icon" {{ ...dropdown_menu_trigger_attrs }}>` is what I would recommend.
- Menu still open after going back: the menu did not close when an item was activated, so bfcache restored it open. Activating an item now closes the menu (like Radix does), which also fixes the back navigation case.

**Sidebar**

- `DropdownMenu:Content` gained `side` (`top`/`right`/`bottom`/`left`) and `align` (`start`/`center`/`end`) props. The demo now uses `side="right" align="start"` for the project actions and `side="top"` for the footer menu, so nothing expands off-screen anymore.
- When the sidebar is collapsed to icons, its inner container used `overflow-hidden`, which clipped any open menu. It now stays visible while a dropdown is open, and the menus render above the inset.
- Blocks inside `<twig:Sidebar:Inset>`: not a Sidebar limitation, it is how Twig Components work. The content of a component tag is its own template, and `content` is already the name of its default block, hence the "already defined" error. Blocks declared in there also cannot be overridden through `{% extends %}` (and `outerBlocks` only climbs one level, so it does not help across `Provider > Inset`). The pattern that works is a small layout component that captures its `content` block in a variable and renders it inside the inset:

  ```twig
  {# templates/components/AppLayout.html.twig #}
  {% set page_content %}{% block content %}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
  <twig:Sidebar:Provider>
      <twig:Sidebar>...</twig:Sidebar>
      <twig:Sidebar:Inset>
          ...
          {{ page_content|raw }}
      </twig:Sidebar:Inset>
  </twig:Sidebar:Provider>
  ```

  and then `<twig:AppLayout>...page content...</twig:AppLayout>` inside your pages' `{% block body %}`. I added a "Using the sidebar as a page layout" section to the README with the full snippet, since most people will hit this.

If you get a chance to re-run your scenarios against the new push, I would love to hear how it goes. Thanks again!

